Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:10:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 062/147] hjviewer: the staff-only gate's screens, from the
 user's side

What a user meets around the gate, so that nobody locks a PC out by
surprise and a staff member finds the login first (hjviewer's
docs/access-tickets.md 3-5, 3-6, 5-3):

- A1 is "Staff-only server": [Log in] is the main button, and the access
  password's field opens from "Have an access password?" (at once when the
  build has no login). Its text has no "(access not allowed)": the mark
  stays in the core's msgbox text only. After the access password a toast
  says that the PC's own password comes next.
- A2 has [Reconnect] beside [Close] (not for a port forward).
- The PC home shows its notice above the ID: P1 while hbbs refuses this
  PC; P2's line "until HH:mm" with [End] while the access password's
  ticket holds; on an installed Windows PC without a login, the hint to
  log in (G2), and the login opens once by itself. The status line says
  "Not connected to the server" in the warning's colour while hbbs
  refuses this PC, and so does the tray's tooltip on Windows.
- The app asks GET /api/hjv/access at its start and on each return: on a
  staff-only server the connection pages tell an app without a login to
  log in (G3), and the logout dialog and "Remove from my list" say that
  the PC takes no remote connection until someone logs in on it again,
  as a condition while the mode is unknown, with one more line while the
  PC is used remotely.
- E2 says about how long to wait, from the 429's retry_after; P2's result
  carries when the PC's ticket ends; hjv-guest-pc-end ends it (an empty
  value over the IPC, as before).
- A login in a session window has the main window show what it did with
  this PC, not the session window.

